 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Pre-computation Error:** Calculating uncertainty on coarse predictions *before* sampling yields incorrect values [S1, unofficial]. If `uncertainty_func(logits) = -|logits|`, a point sampled between logits -1 and 1 might have 0 logits, resulting in 0 uncertainty [S1, unofficial]. Pre-computing coarse uncertainties would assign -1 to that point, biasing the selection [S1, unofficial]. Uncertainty must be computed on the logits sampled at the specific random coordinates [S1, unofficial].
